      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that stuff like construction or flow could explain some of it, but the crazy part is how it aligns with my schedule. like if i have a big interview, the green light stays on way longer than it usually does. it feels less like traffic management and more like a prompt. here is what i logged from this morning and yesterday afternoon:\n\nyesterday (tuesday) - big coffee meeting at 2pm:\n- 1:55pm: green light 4th/Pike - 45s\n- 2:05pm: green light 4th/Pike - 62s (way longer than normal)\n- 2:15pm: green light 4th/Pike - 58s\n\ntoday (wednesday) - no big meetings, just errands:\n- 10:30am: green light 4th/Pike - 35s\n- 11:15am: green light 4th/Pike - 38s\n\ncan u look at the timing diffs? does the shift in the green light duration actually seem like it's reacting to the importance of the day or is it just my head? i really need to know if i should be reading into these gaps.",
